<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The identified substantial missingness: weight \(96.9%\) was removed, medical_specialty \(49.1%\) and payer_code \(39.6%\) were retained with an explicit missing category, and question marks were normalised to missing values.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
97 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Administrative *_id fields were handled as categories. 15 medication columns were quasi-constant, but all medication inputs were retained; one-hot encoding groups categories observed fewer than 50 times in the fitting data.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
98 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (Encounters with discharge codes 11, 13, 14, 19, 20, or 21 were excluded as death/hospice stays: 2,423 encounters \(2.4%\). This defines the scope of the proposed follow-up workflow. Hospice exclusion is not evidence that readmission or follow-up is impossible. The retained cohort contains 99,343 encounters with 11.39% positive outcomes. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
99 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
